      "value": "This could potentially cause some issues. I use playspace turn, so if I rotate my viewpoint using OVRAS, it might not be in sync with VRChat or Unity. (For example, playspace mover doesn't move the capsule; it's anchored to the ground.)\nThis suggestion should be a toggle, versus a forced system-wide implementation.\nAnother example where the fun could be ruined in this, is that I like to sneak up behind people, and cover their viewpoint with my hands. If my avatar is disabled, they might not be able to see my avatar.",
